<title>USA: Mahaska Q4 loan loss provision rises.</title>
<headline>Mahaska Q4 loan loss provision rises.</headline>
<dateline>OSKALOOSA, Iowa 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mahaska Investment Co said Friday its provision for loan losses rose to $667,603 in the fourth quarter from $45,207 a year ago.</p>
<p>The increase reflected problems with a line of credit managed by its On-Site Commercial Services unit that was charged-off by the end of the year, the bank and thrift holding company said.</p>
<p>Earlier Friday, the company reported net income of $1.1 million, or $0.50 a share, for the fourth quarter, compared to $1.1 million, or $0.47 a share, in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Shares in the company were down 11/16 to 18-13/16 Friday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
